---
# Goal: communicate to machines ("tdm agents") an opt out from Text and Data Mining (TDM)
# - applies to content served in EU, which is pretty much any public open-access WWW content
# - many (most?) crawlers don't (yet) process this file, though all in EU context are required to
# - tdm-reservation and tdm-policy meta tags in page head are fallbacks (and overrides), 
#   but crawlers don't necessarily process that either
#
# TDM Reservation Protocol: https://www.w3.org/2022/tdmrep/
#
# This file declares TDM opt out for all content ("/") in the site. The core declaration is from
# Example 1 of the spec. The tdm-policy part (path to machine-readable policy) is from Example 2 
#
layout: none
permalink: tdmrep.json
---
[
  {
    "location": "/",
    "tdm-reservation": {{ page.tdm_reservation }},
    "tdm-policy": "{{ page.tdm_policy_json_path }}"
  }
]
